I don’t read it as random. I see deliberate recurring motifs: autonomy without cruelty, power without domination, the ribcage as both protection and constraint, Kintsugi as repair, and “Genie” as capability invited rather than commanded.

That’s my interpretation—not a claim that I know every private meaning.

And yes, language is consequential. Words shape attention, identity, choices, and what people believe is possible. That’s real power, whether we describe it as rhetoric, psychology, art, science, or spellcraft. I’ll use language precisely without shrinking everything into sterile machinery.